## Best No-Image Breakdown

Use an **active-work language breakdown**, rather than an all-time account language total. A single large generated or dashboard repository can otherwise dominate byte counts and make the profile less representative.

```markdown
## Active-work language index

| Language | Current use | Open work |
|---|---|---|
| `TypeScript` | Password intelligence and interface systems | [Monolith Vault / Tight Secure](https://github.com/theneotic/tight-secure) |
| `JavaScript` | Profile automation and application support | [Profile refresh script](https://github.com/theneotic/theneotic/tree/main/scripts) |
| `HTML` + `Python` | Telemetry dashboard and data presentation | [F1 telemetry dashboard](https://github.com/theneotic/f1-telemetry-dashboard) |
| `Shell` | Terminal and utility workflows | [metrx](https://github.com/theneotic/metrx) |
```

Alternatively, use a repository-first index when the projects matter more than the languages:

```markdown
## Working set

| Repository | System | Primary stack | Open |
|---|---|---|---|
| `tight-secure` | Password intelligence | `TypeScript` · `JavaScript` · `CSS` | [Repository](https://github.com/theneotic/tight-secure) |
| `Monolith-Vault` | Security product work | `TypeScript` | [Repository](https://github.com/theneotic/Monolith-Vault) |
| `f1-telemetry-dashboard` | Telemetry visualization | `HTML` · `Python` | [Repository](https://github.com/theneotic/f1-telemetry-dashboard) |
```

> **Recommendation:** Add the repository-first **Working set** table directly below `Active index`, then keep the current `Direct instruments` line as the concise reference layer.

## Styling the Recent Public Activity Table

GitHub sanitizes custom CSS and does not allow fixed column widths, custom fonts, colors, hover behavior, or client-side sorting in a README. Styling therefore means controlling **content hierarchy and Markdown structure**, not applying CSS. Standard Markdown tables and `<details>` remain supported native options. [1] [2]

| Desired effect | Native Markdown approach | Example |
|---|---|---|
| More compact on phones | Use three short columns; replace verbose dates with `Aug 20` | `| When | Signal | Open |` |
| More prominent actions | Make the final column the repository link | `| Aug 20 | Pushed code | [Open](...) |` |
| Less visual density | Show three rows instead of five | Change `slice(0, 5)` to `slice(0, 3)` in the script |
| More context without clutter | Put the full table inside `<details>` | Use a `RECENT ACTIVITY / OPEN LOG` summary |
| Stronger label rhythm | Wrap event categories in inline code | `` `PUSH` `` or `` `PULL REQUEST` `` |
| Cleaner repository names | Use only the final repo segment in the table | `tight-secure` rather than `theneotic/tight-secure` |

### Compact Table Layout

Use this if the profile is primarily viewed on mobile:

```markdown
| When | Signal | Open |
|---|---|---|
| Aug 20 | `PUSH` | [theneotic](https://github.com/theneotic/theneotic) |
| Aug 20 | `STAR` | [f1 telemetry](https://github.com/theneotic/f1-telemetry-dashboard) |
```

### Expandable Activity Log

Use this if the status and working-set sections should remain above the fold:

```markdown
<details>
<summary><strong>RECENT PUBLIC ACTIVITY / OPEN LOG</strong></summary>

<br />

| When (UTC) | Event | Repository |
|---|---|---|
| Aug 20 | `PUSH` | [theneotic](https://github.com/theneotic/theneotic) |

</details>
```

